# Every image in this stack builds from the repository root as its context
# (deploy/gateway.Dockerfile, deploy/loadgen.Dockerfile, and — from M5 —
# worker/Dockerfile, which needs models/fetch.sh).
#
# Without this file that context includes models/download (~365MB of
# weights a developer fetched locally) and worker/.venv, which the daemon
# would tar up and ship on every single build. The weights belong in the
# image, but they get there by fetch.sh running INSIDE the build — never by
# being copied in from a host directory that may hold a different, older,
# or partial set than the one the image claims to have.
.git/
.gitignore

models/download/
models/.cache/

worker/.venv/
worker/.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
*.pyc

/bin/
*.test
/results/

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
